    "description": "The billing application already exposes a synchronous PaymentClient contract whose charge method accepts Money and an idempotency key, then returns a ChargeResult containing a provider-neutral reference and approved status. The only available payment vendor exposes a different API: amounts are decimal major units, currency is represented by vendor enums, submission is asynchronous and completes through a callback, and failures arrive as vendor-specific status objects. Business code must continue using the existing contract, and vendor types are forbidden from crossing the billing module. One implementation of PaymentClient must translate units and identifiers, reconcile the callback lifecycle, and map all documented failures into the target error contract. It must not add tax calculation, persistence, retries, or capabilities the vendor does not provide, and the vendor SDK cannot be changed. Integration tests must be able to exercise the application contract without loading the vendor library.",
    "decision_statement": "Choose where to preserve the billing application's existing synchronous charge contract while translating the vendor SDK's major-unit, callback-based protocol without leaking vendor types or adding unrelated behavior.",
    "notes": "adapter fits preserving the synchronous charge contract while translating the vendor's major-unit callback protocol; wrapper-facade and facade are near misses for the ownership-entry axes, with interface-class supporting the contract. Fixed: reworded 'bridge the callback lifecycle' to remove the family term 'bridge'."
  },
